          <item>
          <widget class="QLabel" name="label_windowSnapExplanation">
            <property name="text">
              <string>While you move a window, KWin's own window snapping pulls it against the edges of nearby windows (System Settings / Window Management / Window Behavior / Movement / Window snap zone). The guides show which window it is snapping to. When activated by a screen corner, reaching that corner while moving a window switches the rest of that move to the guides, hiding the zone selector, zone overlay and edge snapping.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
              <bool>true</bool>
            </property>
